    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640-a2">

                <pb facs="0728" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg648"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Canal to Mr.
                            Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Haiti</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: The Provisional Government has
                    been advised that ex-Admiral Killick, at present in rebellion against the
                    legitimate authority, has seized on board of the German merchant steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Markomannia</hi> some arms and ammunitions shipped from
                    the capital for Cape Haiti.</p>
                <p>Already the Provisional Government has made it its duty to protest against the
                    so-called blockade of the latter city; it again comes to protest against the
                    acts of Mr. Killick, who has made a material attack on the right which foreign
                    vessels have of entering the ports of the Republic open to commerce and to
                    freely leave.</p>
                <p>It is a real depredation, an act of piracy, to which I have the honor to call
                    your attention, in begging you at the same time to take all measures to prevent
                    the recurrence.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boisrond Canal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
